# 8. SALESFLO KPI SCORECARD FOR N-LINK

Implement a configurable performance engine.

Recommended KPI framework:

| KPI | Suggested Weight |
|---|---:|
| Outlet Productivity | 20% |
| Call Productivity | 15% |
| Bill Productivity | 20% |
| SKU per Bill | 15% |
| Strike Rate | 20% |
| Visit Compliance | 10% |
| Total | 100% |

These are suggested defaults only.

Management must be able to configure targets, weightage, reporting period, thresholds and applicable roles.

## KPI formulas

Outlet Productivity:

Unique outlets served / assigned outlet target × 100.

Call Productivity:

Completed valid calls / assigned call target × 100.

Bill Productivity:

Productive invoices / assigned bill target × 100.

Strike Rate:

Productive calls / valid total calls × 100.

SKU per Bill:

Total eligible SKU lines / eligible invoices.

Visit Compliance:

Valid completed visits / planned visits × 100.

Define edge cases, zero denominators, cancelled invoices, duplicate visits and rejected transactions.

Do not count draft orders as completed bills.

Do not count unverified visits.

Do not count cancelled invoices as sales.

## Scorecard interface

Each KPI card must show:

- KPI name
- Weightage
- Target
- Achievement
- Achievement percentage
- Points earned
- Previous period comparison
- Expandable calculation
- Underlying source records

Provide:

Daily, Weekly, MTD and Custom Date Range.

Provide OB-wise and TSM-wise comparison.

Allow authorized management to inspect the exact calculation behind every score.

