# 14. BACKEND AND DATABASE INTEGRATION

Preserve the existing Supabase architecture.

Do not rebuild the database unnecessarily.

Review existing tables, migrations, views, functions, triggers and RLS policies before adding anything.

All mobile and desktop screens must read the same authoritative records.

Core transaction rules:

## Sales

Approved Order → Invoice → Stock Out → Ledger Debit → Dispatch.

## Recovery

Recovery Entry → Verification → Ledger Credit.

## Return

Return Request → Approval → Receipt → Inspection → Inventory Adjustment → Credit Note → Ledger.

## Attendance

Real Device GPS → Server Validation → Attendance Record → Audit History.

## Visits

Assigned Customer → Visit Start → GPS Validation → Activity → Outcome → Visit Completion.

## Inventory

Opening Stock + Approved Stock In - Approved Stock Out = Current Stock.

## Customer Ledger

Opening Balance + Debits - Credits = Closing Balance.

Never update financial balances directly.

Use controlled atomic transactions.

Use idempotency keys for mobile retries.

Preserve audit history and reversal workflows.

